
# Java 8 Lambda & Streams -

## 1. Lambda Expression

### Definition

Lambda Expression is a short way to implement a Functional Interface.

### Syntax

```java
(parameters) -> { logic }
```

### Examples

```java
() -> System.out.println("Hello");

name -> System.out.println(name);

(a,b) -> a + b;
```

### Benefits

* Less code
* Improves readability
* Used heavily with Streams

---

## 2. Functional Interface

### Definition

An interface having exactly one abstract method.

```java
@FunctionalInterface
interface Greeting {
    void sayHello();
}
```

### Rules

* Only one abstract method
* Can have multiple default methods
* Can have multiple static methods

### Examples

* Runnable
* Comparator
* Predicate
* Function
* Consumer
* Supplier

---

## 3. Built-in Functional Interfaces

| Interface     | Input | Output  | Method   |
| ------------- | ----- | ------- | -------- |
| Predicate<T>  | Yes   | boolean | test()   |
| Consumer<T>   | Yes   | No      | accept() |
| Supplier<T>   | No    | Yes     | get()    |
| Function<T,R> | Yes   | Yes     | apply()  |

### Examples

```java
Predicate<Integer> p = n -> n > 10;

Consumer<String> c = name -> System.out.println(name);

Supplier<String> s = () -> "Hello";

Function<String,Integer> f = str -> str.length();
```

